# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# GATE-HYGIENE: description strings must contain NO dollar-sign and NO backtick (set -u in the runner).
register_gate "tests/test_api_recall.py" "API RECALL GATE: PASS" "API-contract / OpenAPI cross-substrate RECALL (coverage holes) + multi-definer precision regression-lock" "API-contract + OpenAPI cross-substrate recall: the precision fixes #329 (openapi multi-definer suppression) and #332 (api-contract graphql/proto multi-definer suppression + stoplists) removed a real false-couple class; this gate measures the OPPOSITE failure they could have caused (over-suppression dropping a genuine single-definer contract) plus real contract shapes never extracted at all, on crafted temp repos (offline, no Postgres, no PyYAML dependency -- JSON spec). RECALL HOLES FIXED: (R1) GraphQL extend type X -- a type split across files via extend (schema stitching / federation) is ONE contract; before the fix the extension was counted as a 2nd DEFINER so the multi-definer guard suppressed the whole type and the base, the extension and every referencer silently lost coupling; fix routes an extension to a reference (queries) edge, not a definer (alters) edge, so base+extension+fan-out couple while a genuine 2-bare-base-def type remains inert ambiguous evidence. (R2) OpenAPI template-literal path -- a frontend that builds a REST path with a JS/TS template literal (the most common frontend path form) normalized differently from the spec brace form and the spec-to-frontend path coupling was silently dropped; fix collapses the template interpolation to a placeholder like the brace/colon styles. (R3) OpenAPI 3.1 webhooks -- a webhook operationId defined in the spec and implemented by a backend handler is a real contract that the parser ignored (only the paths block was read); fix extracts webhook operationId operations (operationId only, since a webhook key is an event name, not a URL path, so no bogus path anchor). PRECISION REGRESSION-LOCKS (the #329/#332 gains must hold): single-definer crown jewels still couple (GraphQL type Order, proto service OrderService) and a genuine multi-definer remains persisted but excluded from effective adjacency (the SAME bare type/message in two files, and an extend does NOT rescue a genuinely 2-base-def type). Coupling is read exactly as the product reads it: shared-resource adjacency consumes only alters/queries edges whose reference_status is NULL. Content-free: api symbol names + file paths only. Recall-safe: uncertainty is kept as evidence and never converted to a resolved coupling. Proven as a real regression-lock: it FAILS on the pre-fix modules (R1/R2/R3) and PASSES on the fixed ones." "API-contract / OpenAPI cross-substrate recall holes are closed without undoing the multi-definer precision gains: a GraphQL extend-split type, a frontend template-literal REST path, and an OpenAPI 3.1 webhook operation now produce the real cross-file coupling, while single-definer crown jewels still couple and genuine multi-definer name collisions remain inert evidence." 14
